            <title xml:id="title_4bdb12fa" xml:lang="de">Concerto a cembalo obligato, violino 1mo, violino 2do, viola et basso</title>
            <contributor xml:id="respStmt_c15f0917">
               <persName role="composer" xml:id="persName_d0ce6426">Johann Adolph Scheibe</persName>
            </contributor>
            <history xml:id="history_b9848e89">
               <p xml:id="idm207">The present concerto for obligato harpsichord and strings – the only one to have survived for that combination – was composed sometime before 1745 when the latest transcript was dated and carried out in Darmstadt. The earliest set of parts (<rend xml:id="idm208" fontstyle="italic">D-B</rend>, BP 656) shows signs of having been a working copy rather than a fair copy as the harpsichord part in particular contains numerous changes and corrections which are included in the second set of parts.</p>
            </history>
